No. QOS Portable is designed to run on FreeBSD/arm64 without any installed software in the guest environment. It is not a Linux program but a portable host that boots a native kernel and executes FP-RISC applications directly.

```sol
// Example of a QOS Portable application running on a FreeBSD/arm64 guest
import qos;

func main() {
    // QOS Portable handles the boot and HAL table setup automatically
    // No explicit Linux-specific code is required here
    print "Hello from QOS Portable";
}
```

